-- The hostile reading: one block per finding in NOTES.md section 4 that the encoding can
-- demonstrate. Each assertion states the SURPRISING answer the wording gives, and passes; a
-- finding marked "reading only" in NOTES.md has no block here. Fixtures come from
-- uic-par-tests.l4; every money figure is hypothetical (VND).

§ `Findings`

§§ `Finding 1 — "nổi loạn" is saved by the carve-back to B1 and excluded by A3(b)`

-- src:202 | nhưng Hợp đồng bảo hiểm này sẽ không loại trừ Tổn thất (với điều kiện là những tổn thất này
-- src:203 | không bị loại trừ bởi các quy định khác) gây ra bởi cháy, sét đánh, nổ, máy bay rơi, nổi loạn, bãi
-- src:204 | công, công nhân bế xưởng, những người tham dự vào các cuộc gây rối lao động, những người
-- src:123 | (b) nổi dậy, bạo động dân sự có tính chất hoặc dẫn đến nổi dậy quần chúng, binh biến, khởi
-- src:124 | nghĩa, nổi loạn, cách mạng, hành động quân sự hoặc tiếm quyền;
-- Fixed glass broken in a "nổi loạn": B1's carve-back saves it, A3(b) excludes it.
#ASSERT NOT `exclusion B1(b)-(d) applies to` (`property of kind` `fixed glass` `, specially stated` FALSE `, damaged by` `riot or rebellion`)
#ASSERT `the exclusions that apply to` (`property of kind` `fixed glass` `, specially stated` FALSE `, damaged by` `riot or rebellion`) EQUALS LIST "A3(b)"
-- And on stock: a strike is covered, a "nổi loạn" never is.
#ASSERT `an exclusion applies to` (`stock damaged directly by` `riot or rebellion`)
#ASSERT NOT `an exclusion applies to` (`stock damaged directly by` `strike`)

§§ `Finding 2 — three regimes for property insured elsewhere`

-- (i) "insured separately under another, separate policy": excluded outright (B3(i)).
#ASSERT `exclusion B3(i) applies to` (`stock damaged by` `fire` `, being` `insured separately under another, separate policy`)
-- (ii) insured by another policy in force: B4 leaves the excess (40 of 100), then General
-- Condition 6 caps it at a "rateable proportion" it never defines: the answer is a refusal.
#ASSERT `exclusion B4: the part of` 100_000_000 `this Policy bears, given` (`insured by other policies in force at the time of the Loss` 60_000_000) EQUALS 40_000_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount the Policy pays for` `a June Loss to stock also insured elsewhere for 60 million` `under` `the test policy` BECAUSE "General Condition 6 does not say how the rateable proportion is measured"
-- (iii) B4 measures this Policy's share by what the other policy would have paid ALONE (60).
-- If that other policy carries its own rateable-proportion clause and pays by sums insured
-- (60 of 160, so 37.5), while this Policy holds the Insured to the B4 excess (40, which is
-- also under a sum-insured share of 100/160 = 62.5), the Insured recovers 77.5 of a 100 loss.
#ASSERT `General Condition 6, on a supplied basis: no more than` (100 DIVIDED BY 160) `of a loss of` 100_000_000 EQUALS 62_500_000
#ASSERT (min 40_000_000 62_500_000) PLUS (100_000_000 TIMES 60 DIVIDED BY 160) EQUALS 77_500_000

§§ `Finding 3 — General Condition 12 cuts short the three months of General Condition 4(b)`

-- A Loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on 1 July, rejected on 1 May 2027, action begun on 15 July
-- 2027: inside the three months 4(b) allows (to 1 August 2027), and still barred, because on
-- 15 June 2027 the claim was neither pending nor in arbitration.
`a claim rejected on 1 May 2027 and sued on 15 July 2027` MEANS
    `a claim` (YMD 2026 6 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 5 1)) (JUST (YMD 2027 7 15)) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `General Condition 4(b): the last day to begin an action, three months after` (YMD 2027 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 8 1
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 4(b): all benefit is forfeited, as at` (YMD 2027 7 20) `, for` `a claim rejected on 1 May 2027 and sued on 15 July 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 12: the Insurer can still be liable, as at` (YMD 2027 7 20) `, for a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `under` `a claim rejected on 1 May 2027 and sued on 15 July 2027`
#ASSERT `the amount the Insurer owes, as at` (YMD 2027 7 20) `, for` `the June fire` `under` `the test policy` `on` `a claim rejected on 1 May 2027 and sued on 15 July 2027` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 4 — General Condition 7 counts one default from two days`

-- Request made 31 July 2026 and received 30 August (a month in the post): the party asked is
-- late from 1 October, and the other may appoint a sole arbitrator only from 31 October.
#ASSERT `General Condition 7: the days on which the party asked is late but no sole arbitrator may yet be appointed, for a request made on` (YMD 2026 7 31) `and received on` (YMD 2026 8 30) EQUALS 30

§§ `Finding 6 — the Insurer's opinion alone shifts the burden of proof`

#ASSERT `who must prove that the loss is covered, under Exclusion A3, where` FALSE `and where` TRUE EQUALS `the Insured bears it`

§§ `Finding 7 — an innocent misdescription takes the property out of cover`

#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` `stock burnt, misdescribed`) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 8 — any change of trade ends cover, even one that lowers the risk`

#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` (`stock burnt after` `the trade or manufacture carried on was altered` `, with consent endorsed` FALSE)) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 9 — terms with no stated consequence`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount the Insurer owes, as at` (YMD 2026 8 1) `, for` `the June fire` `under` `the test policy` `on` (`a claim` (YMD 2026 6 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 7 16)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "General Condition 9 was not complied with, and the wording does not say whether that defeats the claim"

§§ `Finding 10 — two vacancy rules`

-- Escaping water on the fifth day the building stands empty: excluded (A1(c)(vi)).
#ASSERT `an exclusion applies to` (`stock damaged by` `bursting, overflowing, discharge or leakage of water from tanks, apparatus or pipes` `, being` `in a building that was empty or not in use`)
-- Fire on the fifth day: covered (General Condition 8(b) needs more than 30 days).
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 8: cover had ended before the loss on` (`stock burnt after` (`the building had been unoccupied, for this many days, when the loss happened` 5) `, with consent endorsed` FALSE)
-- Fire on the thirty-first day: nothing, for any cause.
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` (`stock burnt after` (`the building had been unoccupied, for this many days, when the loss happened` 31) `, with consent endorsed` FALSE)) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 11 — the insuring clause names no first day`

-- Premium paid 20 December 2025; Period from 1 January 2026; loss on 25 December 2025.
#ASSERT `the insuring clause's own words reach a Loss on` (YMD 2025 12 25) `under` `the test policy`
#ASSERT NOT `the cover was running on` (YMD 2025 12 25) `under` `the test policy`

§§ `Finding 12 — the deductible comes off after the limit`

-- The June fire, 3,952m of covered loss, a 3,000m limit and a 50m deductible: 2,950m. On the
-- other order (deductible first, then the cap) it would be 3,000m.
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` `the June fire` `under` (`a 2026 policy` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 20)) EMPTY (JUST 3_000_000_000) (JUST 50_000_000) `not terminated`) EQUALS 2_950_000_000
#ASSERT min (3_952_000_000 MINUS 50_000_000) 3_000_000_000 EQUALS 3_000_000_000

§§ `Finding 13 — a sum insured, once paid, is gone for the rest of the Period`

-- Stock insured for 2,000m was paid in full in March; restocked, it burns in June: nothing.
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a Loss on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `to` (LIST (`a loss under` `item 3, stock` 2_000_000_000 2_000_000_000 `no other insurance` (LIST (`stock damaged directly by` `fire`)))) `, after earlier payments of` 2_000_000_000) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 14 — the Insured who cancels cannot know the refund`

#ASSERT REFUSED `General Condition 3: the premium to be refunded under` (`a 2026 policy` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 20)) EMPTY NOTHING NOTHING (`terminated at the Insured's written request, with effect from` (YMD 2026 9 1))) BECAUSE "the customary short-period rates by which General Condition 3 charges the Insured who ends the Policy are not stated in the wording"

§§ `Finding 15 — one fraudulent claim forfeits every claim`

-- The June fire claim is honest; a later claim on another loss was fraudulent: the June fire
-- pays nothing.
#ASSERT `the amount the Insurer owes, as at` (YMD 2026 8 1) `, for` `the June fire` `under` `the test policy` `on` (`a claim` (YMD 2026 6 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) NOTHING TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 16 — A1(b) and A1(d) have no exception for subsequent loss`

-- src:51 | trừ những Tổn thất do những nguyên nhân không bị loại trừ trong Hợp đồng bảo hiểm
-- src:52 | phát sinh sau đó và trong trường hợp này Công ty bảo hiểm chỉ chịu trách nhiệm đối với
-- src:53 | các Tổn thất phát sinh sau đó.
-- Wear and tear that starts a fire: the fire damage is paid (A1(a)'s exception).
#ASSERT NOT `an exclusion applies to` (`stock damaged by` `fire` `after` `wear and tear`)
-- Rust that starts a fire: the fire damage is excluded (A1(b) has no such exception).
#ASSERT `exclusion A1(b) applies to` (`stock damaged by` `fire` `after` `corrosion or rust`)
-- A landslip that ruptures a gas main and starts a fire: excluded (A1(d)).
#ASSERT `exclusion A1(d) applies to` (`stock damaged by` `fire` `after` `subsidence, ground movement or landslip`)
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` (`stock damaged by` `fire` `after` `corrosion or rust`)) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 18 — a forecast storm is not a "Tổn thất"`

-- A typhoon forecast days ahead damages the building: physical, accidental, sudden, but not
-- unforeseen. The defined term requires all four (fork F3), so the storm the B1 carve-back
-- names is not paid.
`a forecast typhoon` MEANS
    `The Loss` WITH
        `the date of the Loss`       IS YMD 2026 9 20
        `physical`                   IS TRUE
        `accidental`                 IS TRUE
        `sudden`                     IS TRUE
        `unforeseen`                 IS FALSE
        `the losses under each item` IS LIST (`a loss under` `item 1, buildings` 9_000_000_000 0 `no other insurance` (LIST (`property of kind` `a building` `, specially stated` FALSE `, damaged by` `storm`)))
        `the amount already paid for earlier losses in the period` IS 0
#ASSERT NOT `an exclusion applies to` (`property of kind` `a building` `, specially stated` FALSE `, damaged by` `storm`)
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` `a forecast typhoon` `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 19 — theft is covered only by forcible entry or exit at a building`

#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` (`stock damaged directly by` `theft`)) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount the Policy pays for` (`a June Loss to stock of` (`stock damaged by` `theft` `, being` `stolen at a building with force and violence used to enter it or to escape from it`)) `under` `the test policy` EQUALS 50_000_000
